+*   **Boundaries:** Far clipping plane must be handled to prevent infinite loops or invalid hits [G].
+*   **Degenerate Input:** If `TraceDistance` is zero or `RadiusPixel` is zero, division by zero occurs in alpha calculation [G]. Guard against this [G].
+*   **Material ID Consistency:** The represent hit only updates if the material ID matches the current hit or is uninitialized (-1) [S1, unofficial]. This prevents mixing materials in the represent pass [G].
+*   **Hit Distance Offset:** The hit distance must be calculated as $t + \text{currentMap}.x$ rather than $t$ to avoid underestimating the true intersection point by the adaptive epsilon margin [G].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N_{steps})$ per pixel, where $N_{steps}$ is the maximum number of sphere tracing iterations. The represent hit logic adds constant overhead per step.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ per pixel for hit records. Requires two render targets (surface and represent).
